          "label": "Who is who in Maria's life?",
          "strip": [],
          "text": "Maria is thirty-two and lives in a small flat in Vilnius. She shares it with her {1}, a student called Eva, who pays half of the rent. At work, her {2} Tom sits at the next desk and always helps her with the computer. On Tuesday evenings she goes to an Italian course, where her {3} Paolo lets her copy his notes. Her {4}, Lina, has known her since school, and they talk almost every day. Maria was married once, but she and her {5}, Jonas, got divorced three years ago. Before him she had a {6} called Marek; they only went out for a year, and he now lives in Spain. Her brother Paul broke up with Kate last spring, so Kate is now his {7}, although she still sends Maria a card every birthday. Maria's neighbours, Ben and Ola, are a lovely {8}: they have been together for fifty years. And Maria? She has a new {9} now, Daniel, and next month they are moving in together.",
